@startuml
!theme plain
!pragma layout elk
title TASK-260715-1q4qhw — system state and provider capability authority

state "Owned disabled" as Disabled
state "System disconnected" as Ready
state "System connecting" as Connecting
state "System reasserting" as Reasserting
state "System disconnecting" as Disconnecting
state "System invalid" as Invalid

state "System connected" as Connected {
  state "Capability unknown" as Unknown
  state "Provider TCP + safe DNS" as Degraded
  state "Provider TCP + safe DNS + UDP" as Capabilities

  [*] --> Unknown : NEVPNStatus.connected\nrequires fresh query
  Unknown --> Degraded : fresh healthy compatible snapshot\nroutes + TCP + safe DNS
  Unknown --> Capabilities : fresh healthy compatible snapshot\nroutes + TCP + safe DNS + UDP
  Degraded --> Capabilities : newer current-generation snapshot adds UDP
  Capabilities --> Degraded : newer snapshot removes UDP; safety remains
}

[*] --> Disabled
Disabled --> Ready : explicit enable + save + reload
Ready --> Disabled : explicit disable + save + reload
Ready --> Connecting : session accepts start
Connecting --> Connected : NEVPNStatus.connected
Connecting --> Ready : disconnected / start failure
Connecting --> Invalid : NEVPNStatus.invalid
Connected --> Reasserting : NEVPNStatus.reasserting
Reasserting --> Connected : NEVPNStatus.connected\ncapability resets to unknown
Connected --> Disconnecting : stop
Reasserting --> Disconnecting : stop
Connecting --> Disconnecting : stop
Connected --> Ready : disconnected / system failure
Reasserting --> Ready : disconnected / system failure
Disconnecting --> Ready : NEVPNStatus.disconnected
Disconnecting --> Invalid : NEVPNStatus.invalid
Ready --> Invalid : observed NEVPNStatus.invalid
Invalid --> Disabled : fresh reload finds owned disabled
Invalid --> Ready : fresh reload finds owned enabled/disconnected

note right of Connected
NETunnelProviderSession is connected authority.
Only a fresh provider snapshot supplies capability facts.
Every non-connected status clears all capability claims.
end note

note right of Capabilities
Provider facts only; final UX wording is reserved.
end note
@enduml
